/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Ports 1 and 2 are the ends of the through (collinear) guide and port 3 is the branch.
   - With the branch matched (S₃₃ = 0), the usual matrices are
   - rows and columns are ports 1, 2, 3.
   - S₁₁ = S₂₂ = ½: a collinear port reflects a quarter of the power fed into it.
   - Suppose a lossless reciprocal three-port were matched: S₁₁ = S₂₂ = S₃₃ = 0.
   - So a real tee always reflects at some port.
   - A magic tee (hybrid tee) is an E-plane and an H-plane branch on the same junction.
   - rows and columns are ports 1, 2, 3 (H), 4 (E).
   - Some syllabi list corners, bends and twists with tees, because tee arms reach their loads through them.
*/
