/* book Worked example: Q: A directional coupler with 10 dB coupling and 20 dB directivity is fed with 20 dBm at port 1; all other ports are matched. Find the power at the coupled, isolated and through ports in dBm and mW.
   1. Input P₁ = 20 dBm = 1020/10 mW = 100 mW.
   2. Coupled port: P₃ = P₁ − C = 20 − 10 = 10 dBm = 10 mW.
   3. Isolation I = C + D = 10 + 20 = 30 dB, so P₄ = 20 − 30 = −10 dBm = 0.1 mW.
   4. Through port (lossless coupler): P₂ = 100 − 10 − 0.1 = 89.9 mW = 10 log₁₀ 89.9 = 19.54 dBm, a coupling loss of 0.46 dB.
   Answer: P₃ = 10 dBm (10 mW), P₄ = −10 dBm (0.1 mW), P₂ = 19.54 dBm (89.9 mW). */
